WEBVTT

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:09.800
What the?!

00:02:57.633 --> 00:02:59.900
Okay, i think i found a way

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:01.900
We can bypass that
construction just east of here.

00:03:01.934 --> 00:03:05.067
We might even make pennsylvania
faster than we thought.

00:03:05.101 --> 00:03:06.501
Yeah.

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:08.800
Problem is we're not
going to pennsylvania.

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:10.834
Wait... what?

00:03:10.867 --> 00:03:13.267
I just got a call from an old friend.

00:03:13.301 --> 00:03:15.267
Her father was killed last night.

00:03:15.301 --> 00:03:16.800
She thinks it might
be our kind of thing.

00:03:16.834 --> 00:03:18.000
What?

00:03:18.034 --> 00:03:19.434
Yeah, believe me,

00:03:19.468 --> 00:03:22.934
<i>She never would've called,
never, if she didn't need us.</i>

00:03:24.967 --> 00:03:26.900
Come on. You coming or what?

00:03:38.134 --> 00:03:40.633
By "old friend," you mean...

00:03:40.667 --> 00:03:42.900
A friend that's not new.

00:03:42.934 --> 00:03:44.134
Yeah, thanks.

00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:47.468
So, her name's cassie, huh?

00:03:47.501 --> 00:03:49.201
You never mentioned her.

00:03:49.234 --> 00:03:51.267
Didn't i? No.

00:03:51.301 --> 00:03:53.934
Yeah, we went out. You
mean you dated someone?

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:57.234
For more than one night?

00:03:57.267 --> 00:03:59.900
Am i speaking a language
you're not getting here?

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:02.401
Dad and i were working
a job in athens, ohio.

00:04:02.434 --> 00:04:05.301
She was finishing up college.
We went out for a couple weeks.

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:06.934
And?

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:12.000
Look, it's terrible about her dad,

00:04:12.034 --> 00:04:14.667
But it kind of sounds like
a standard car accident.

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:16.967
I'm not seeing how it
fits with what we do.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:20.201
Which, by the way, how
does she know what we do?

00:04:24.733 --> 00:04:27.667
You told her. You told her the secret.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.667
Our big family rule number one...

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.967
We do what we do and
we shut up about it.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.600
For a year and a half, i do
nothing but lie to jessica,

00:04:34.633 --> 00:04:37.301
And you go out with this
chick in ohio a couple of times

00:04:37.334 --> 00:04:39.568
And you tell her everything?

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:40.600
Dean!

00:04:40.633 --> 00:04:42.600
Yeah, looks like.

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:49.234
Anderson: It's a
newspaper we put out here,

00:04:49.235 --> 00:04:51.067
Not a bulletin for the mayor's office.

00:04:51.101 --> 00:04:52.867
Get off your soapbox, jimmy.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:55.134
I'm urging a little discretion is all.

00:04:55.167 --> 00:04:58.234
No, i think you're telling
us what you want us to print

00:04:58.267 --> 00:05:00.167
And what you want us to sit on.

00:05:00.201 --> 00:05:01.967
I know you're upset, cassie.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.600
I liked your dad a lot.

00:05:03.633 --> 00:05:07.000
But i think your grief
is clouding your judgment.

00:05:07.034 --> 00:05:09.867
Two black people were killed
on the same stretch of road

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:11.667
In the same way in three weeks.

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.468
Jimmy, you're too close to this.

00:05:13.501 --> 00:05:15.900
Those guys were friends of yours.

00:05:15.934 --> 00:05:21.301
Again, i'm very sorry for your loss.

00:05:30.733 --> 00:05:33.234
Dean.

00:05:33.267 --> 00:05:34.834
Hey, cassie.

00:05:40.934 --> 00:05:43.201
This is my brother, sam.

00:05:46.967 --> 00:05:48.568
I'm sorry about your dad.

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:52.468
Yeah, me, too.

00:05:56.267 --> 00:05:59.101
My mother's in pretty bad shape.

00:05:59.134 --> 00:06:00.767
I've been staying with her.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:03.267
I wish she wouldn't go off by herself.

00:06:03.301 --> 00:06:05.667
She's been snervous and frightened.

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:07.301
She was worried about dad.

00:06:07.334 --> 00:06:08.667
Why?

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:09.700
He was scared.

00:06:09.733 --> 00:06:11.267
He was seeing things.

00:06:11.301 --> 00:06:12.568
Like what?

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:15.468
He swore he saw an awful-Looking
black truck following him.

00:06:15.501 --> 00:06:17.867
A truck? Who was the driver?

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:20.900
He didn't talk about a
driver, just the truck.

00:06:20.934 --> 00:06:23.501
He said it would appear and disappear.

00:06:23.534 --> 00:06:26.367
And in the accident,
dad's truck was dented

00:06:26.401 --> 00:06:29.501
Like it had been slammed
into by something big.

00:06:29.534 --> 00:06:30.733
Thanks.

00:06:30.767 --> 00:06:34.301
Now, you're sure this
dent wasn't there before?

00:06:34.334 --> 00:06:36.367
He sold cars, always drove a new one.

00:06:36.401 --> 00:06:38.468
There wasn't a scratch on that thing.

00:06:38.501 --> 00:06:42.301
It had rained hard that night.
There was mud everywhere.

00:06:42.334 --> 00:06:47.034
There was a distinct set of
muddy tracks from dad's car

00:06:47.067 --> 00:06:50.101
Leading right...

00:06:50.134 --> 00:06:53.101
To the edge where he went over.

00:06:54.501 --> 00:06:57.334
One set of tracks... his.

00:06:57.367 --> 00:07:00.034
And the first person killed
was a friend of your father's?

00:07:00.067 --> 00:07:01.468
Best friend... clayton solmes.

00:07:01.501 --> 00:07:03.201
They owned a car dealership together.

00:07:03.234 --> 00:07:07.101
Same thing... dent, no tracks.

00:07:07.134 --> 00:07:10.600
And the cops said exactly
what they said about dad...

00:07:10.633 --> 00:07:12.301
"He lost control of his car."

00:07:12.334 --> 00:07:14.534
Can you think of why your father
and partner might be targets?

00:07:14.568 --> 00:07:16.000
No.

00:07:16.034 --> 00:07:18.034
You think this vanishing
truck ran him off the road?

00:07:18.067 --> 00:07:21.767
When you say it aloud like that...

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:27.134
Listen, i'm a little skeptical
about this ghost stuff

00:07:27.167 --> 00:07:29.667
Or whatever it is you guys are into.

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:31.201
Skeptical.

00:07:31.234 --> 00:07:33.700
If i remember, i think
you said i was nuts.

00:07:33.733 --> 00:07:35.568
That was then.

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:37.867
Hmm.

00:07:39.867 --> 00:07:42.468
I just know that i can't
explain what happened up there,

00:07:42.501 --> 00:07:44.167
So i called you.

00:07:45.733 --> 00:07:48.468
Mom. Where have you been?

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:52.534
I had no idea you'd
invited friends over.

00:07:52.568 --> 00:07:56.900
Mom, this is dean, a friend
of mine from... college,

00:07:56.934 --> 00:07:59.468
And his brother, sam.

00:07:59.501 --> 00:08:03.800
Well, l-L-L-I
won't interrupt you.

00:08:03.834 --> 00:08:05.067
Mrs. Robinson? Hmm?

00:08:05.101 --> 00:08:07.534
We're sorry for your loss.

00:08:07.568 --> 00:08:10.534
We'd like to talk to you for
a minute, if you don't mind.

00:08:10.568 --> 00:08:14.900
I'm really not up to that just now.

00:09:10.301 --> 00:09:12.900
Dd: Jimmy meant something to this town.

00:09:12.934 --> 00:09:14.633
He was one of our best.

00:09:14.667 --> 00:09:17.167
It won't be the same without him.

00:09:17.201 --> 00:09:20.134
Our best seem to be dropping like flies.

00:09:20.167 --> 00:09:22.000
Clayton, my father, jimmy.

00:09:22.034 --> 00:09:24.800
What is it exactly you want me to do?

00:09:24.834 --> 00:09:28.800
Well, how about closing this
section of road for starters?

00:09:28.834 --> 00:09:31.000
Close the main road, the
only road in and out of town?

00:09:31.034 --> 00:09:35.134
Accidents happen, cassie. That's
what they are... accidents.

00:09:35.167 --> 00:09:37.568
Did the cops check for
denting on jimmy's car

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:39.234
To see if it was pushed?

00:09:39.267 --> 00:09:40.434
Who's this?

00:09:40.468 --> 00:09:43.401
Dean and sam winchester, family friends.

00:09:43.434 --> 00:09:46.568
This is mayor harold todd.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:49.767
There's one set of tracks...
one. Doesn't point to foul play.

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:52.101
Mayor, the police and town officials

00:09:52.134 --> 00:09:53.867
Take their cues from you...
if you're indifferent about...

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:55.167
Indifferent?

00:09:55.201 --> 00:09:58.034
Would you close the road
if the victims were white?

00:09:58.067 --> 00:10:00.867
You're suggesting i'm racist, cassie.

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:04.434
I'm the last person you
should talk to like that.

00:10:04.468 --> 00:10:05.434
Why is that?

00:10:05.468 --> 00:10:07.667
Why don't you k your mother?

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:16.534
I'll say this for her... she's fearless.

00:10:16.568 --> 00:10:17.600
Mm-Hmm.

00:10:17.633 --> 00:10:21.134
Bet she kicked your ass a coupleimes.

00:10:21.167 --> 00:10:24.800
What's interesting is you guys
never really look at each other

00:10:24.834 --> 00:10:25.934
At the same time.

00:10:25.967 --> 00:10:28.401
You look at her when she's not looking.

00:10:28.434 --> 00:10:30.834
She checks you out when you look away.

00:10:32.367 --> 00:10:36.201
It's just a... just an
interesting observation

00:10:36.234 --> 00:10:39.834
In a, you know,
observationally interesting way.

00:10:39.867 --> 00:10:42.568
You think we might have some
more pressing issues here?

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:44.900
Hey, if i'm hitting a nerve...

00:10:44.934 --> 00:10:46.234
Oh, let's go.

00:11:01.201 --> 00:11:03.401
Excuse me. Are you ron stubbins?

00:11:03.434 --> 00:11:05.234
Friends with jimmy anderson?

00:11:05.267 --> 00:11:06.434
Who are you?

00:11:06.468 --> 00:11:09.067
We're with mr. Anderson's
insurance company.

00:11:09.101 --> 00:11:11.900
Just here to dot some
i's and cross some t's.

00:11:11.934 --> 00:11:14.201
We were just wondering,
had the deceased mentioned

00:11:14.234 --> 00:11:15.767
Any unusual recent experiences?

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:17.234
What do you mean, "unusual"?

00:11:17.267 --> 00:11:19.067
Well, visions, hallucinations.

00:11:19.101 --> 00:11:22.000
It's all part of a medical
examination kind of thing.

00:11:22.034 --> 00:11:24.101
What company you say you were with?

00:11:24.134 --> 00:11:26.434
All tional mutual.

00:11:26.468 --> 00:11:30.034
Tell me, did he ever
mention seeing a truck,

00:11:30.067 --> 00:11:32.034
A big black truck?

00:11:32.067 --> 00:11:34.434
What the hell you talking
about? You even speaking english?

00:11:34.468 --> 00:11:37.867
Son, this truck, a big,
scary, monster-Looking thing?

00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:39.568
Yeah, actually, i think so.

00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:41.633
Hmm.

00:11:41.667 --> 00:11:43.301
What?

00:11:43.334 --> 00:11:44.934
I have heard of a truck like that.

00:11:44.967 --> 00:11:46.234
You have?

00:11:46.267 --> 00:11:47.267
Where?

00:11:47.301 --> 00:11:49.434
Not where... when.

00:11:49.468 --> 00:11:52.800
Back in the '60s, there
was a string of deaths.

00:11:52.834 --> 00:11:55.201
Black men.

00:11:55.234 --> 00:11:59.534
Stores they disappeared in
a big, nasty black truck.

00:11:59.568 --> 00:12:01.067
They ever catch the guy who did it?

00:12:01.101 --> 00:12:02.134
Never found him.

00:12:02.167 --> 00:12:06.800
Hell, not sure they even really looked.

00:12:06.834 --> 00:12:09.000
See, there was a time

00:12:09.034 --> 00:12:15.867
This town wasn't too
friendly to all its citizens.

00:12:18.234 --> 00:12:19.301
Thank you.

00:12:24.101 --> 00:12:25.101
Truck.

00:12:25.134 --> 00:12:26.568
Keeps coming up, doesn't it?

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:28.834
<i>I was thinking. You heard
of the flying dutchman?</i>

00:12:28.867 --> 00:12:31.468
Yeah, a ghost ship infused
with the captain's evil spirit.

00:12:31.501 --> 00:12:33.034
It was basically a part of him.

00:12:33.067 --> 00:12:35.201
So, what if we're dealing
with the same thing?

00:12:35.234 --> 00:12:38.000
A phantom truck who's the
extension of some bastard ghost,

00:12:38.034 --> 00:12:39.201
Re-Enacting past crimes.

00:12:39.234 --> 00:12:41.067
The victims have all been black men.

00:12:41.101 --> 00:12:42.600
I think it's more than that.

00:12:42.633 --> 00:12:45.401
They all seem connected
to cassie and her family.

00:12:45.434 --> 00:12:47.600
All right, well, you work that angle.

00:12:47.633 --> 00:12:48.667
Go talk to her.

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:49.934
Yeah, i will.

00:12:49.967 --> 00:12:52.201
Oh, and you might also want
to mention that other thing.

00:12:52.234 --> 00:12:54.767
What other thing?

00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:57.733
That serious unfinished business.

00:12:57.767 --> 00:13:01.367
Dean, what is going on between you two?

00:13:01.401 --> 00:13:03.834
So maybe we were a little
bit more involved than i said.

00:13:03.867 --> 00:13:06.834
Oh, okay, yeah.

00:13:06.867 --> 00:13:08.900
Okay, a lot more... maybe.

00:13:08.934 --> 00:13:12.034
I told her the secret about
what we do, and i shouldn't have.

00:13:12.067 --> 00:13:15.034
Look, man, everybody's got to
open up to someone sometime.

00:13:15.067 --> 00:13:16.334
Yeah, i don't.

00:13:16.367 --> 00:13:19.600
It was stupid to get that
close. I mean, look how it ended.

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:22.600
Would you stop?

00:13:24.501 --> 00:13:26.468
Blink or something.

00:13:26.501 --> 00:13:28.067
You loved her.

00:13:28.101 --> 00:13:29.234
Oh, god.

00:13:29.267 --> 00:13:33.800
You were in love with
her, but you dumped her.

00:13:36.201 --> 00:13:38.767
Oh, wow.

00:13:40.501 --> 00:13:41.867
She dumped you.

00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:44.700
Get in the car.

00:13:44.733 --> 00:13:46.834
Get in the car!

00:14:02.034 --> 00:14:03.367
Dean.

00:14:03.401 --> 00:14:04.934
Hey. Hey.

00:14:04.967 --> 00:14:07.101
Come on in.

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:12.834
So, you busy?

00:14:12.867 --> 00:14:14.367
The paper is doing a tribute to jimmy.

00:14:14.401 --> 00:14:19.401
I was just going through
his stuff, his awards,

00:14:19.434 --> 00:14:22.334
Trying to find the words.

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:26.167
That's got to be tough.

00:14:26.201 --> 00:14:28.600
For years this family owned
the paper, the dorians.

00:14:28.633 --> 00:14:30.600
They had a whites-Only staff policy.

00:14:30.633 --> 00:14:34.534
After they sold it, jimmy
became the first black reporter.

00:14:34.568 --> 00:14:37.401
He became editor.

00:14:37.434 --> 00:14:39.568
He taught me everything.

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:41.034
Where's your brother?

00:14:42.834 --> 00:14:44.134
Not here.

00:14:44.167 --> 00:14:46.334
All right, so, what brings you here?

00:14:46.367 --> 00:14:48.401
I'm trying to find the connection

00:14:48.434 --> 00:14:49.934
Between the three victims.

00:14:49.967 --> 00:14:51.434
By the way, did you talk to your mom

00:14:51.468 --> 00:14:53.501
About what todd said
about not being a racist?

00:14:53.534 --> 00:14:54.700
I did.

00:14:54.733 --> 00:14:58.000
She didn't want to talk about it.

00:15:00.534 --> 00:15:04.167
So, just then, why did you
ask where my brother was?

00:15:04.201 --> 00:15:05.600
Nothing. Not important.

00:15:05.633 --> 00:15:08.633
Could it be because without
him here it'just you and me

00:15:08.667 --> 00:15:10.501
And not you, me, and sam,
which would be easier?

00:15:10.534 --> 00:15:11.800
It's not easier.

00:15:11.834 --> 00:15:13.501
Look...

00:15:13.534 --> 00:15:16.234
No, forget it. It's fine.

00:15:16.267 --> 00:15:19.301
Keep it strictly business.

00:15:19.334 --> 00:15:21.800
I forgot you do that.

00:15:21.834 --> 00:15:24.367
Do what?

00:15:24.401 --> 00:15:26.767
Oh, whenever we get...

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:29.034
What's the word, close?...

00:15:29.067 --> 00:15:31.834
Anywhere in the neighborhood
of emotional vulnerability,

00:15:31.867 --> 00:15:34.267
You back off or make some joke

00:15:34.301 --> 00:15:36.301
Or find any way to shut the door on me.

00:15:36.334 --> 00:15:38.234
Oh, that's hilarious.

00:15:38.267 --> 00:15:41.034
See, i'm not the one who
took that big, final door

00:15:41.067 --> 00:15:42.867
And slammed it behind
me, and i'm not the one

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:44.367
Who took the key and buried it.

00:15:44.401 --> 00:15:46.101
Are we done with this metaphor?

00:15:46.134 --> 00:15:47.733
All i'm saying is i was totally
up front with you back then

00:15:47.767 --> 00:15:48.800
And you nailed me with it.

00:15:48.834 --> 00:15:50.767
The guy i'm hoping might be in my future

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:52.700
Tells me he professionally pops ghosts.

00:15:52.733 --> 00:15:54.134
Those weren't the words i used.

00:15:54.167 --> 00:15:56.334
And he has to leave too
work with his father. I did.

00:15:56.367 --> 00:15:58.000
All i could think was,
if you want out, fine.

00:15:58.034 --> 00:15:59.967
But don't tell me this insane story.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.401
It was the truth, cassie,

00:16:01.434 --> 00:16:03.900
It didn't sound so insane the
minute you thought i could help.

00:16:03.934 --> 00:16:06.000
Back then i thought you
just wanted to dump me.

00:16:06.034 --> 00:16:08.800
Whoa, let's not forget
who dumped who, okay?

00:16:08.834 --> 00:16:11.000
I thought it was what you wanted.

00:16:11.034 --> 00:16:12.134
Well, it wasn't.

00:16:12.167 --> 00:16:13.967
I didn't mean to hurt you.

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:14.967
Well, you did.

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:16.934
I'm sorry. Yeah, me, too.

00:18:19.367 --> 00:18:22.000
Absolutely.

00:18:22.033 --> 00:18:25.033
Actually, we were always
pretty good at fighting.

00:18:25.067 --> 00:18:27.534
This, we were good at.

00:18:27.567 --> 00:18:31.900
It's all the other stuff, not so much.

00:18:31.933 --> 00:18:34.667
Hey, i tried.

00:18:34.701 --> 00:18:38.734
I told you who i really was.
It was a big first for me.

00:18:38.768 --> 00:18:40.933
Why'd you tell me?

00:18:40.967 --> 00:18:43.367
I don't know.

00:18:46.367 --> 00:18:49.701
I guess i couldn't lie to you.

00:18:52.501 --> 00:18:54.567
Dean...

00:18:54.601 --> 00:18:58.134
When you told me that story,

00:18:58.167 --> 00:18:59.933
It scared the hell out of me.

00:18:59.967 --> 00:19:04.300
I thought you were nuts, dangerous even.

00:19:04.334 --> 00:19:07.933
Actually...

00:19:07.967 --> 00:19:12.267
Maybe i was looking for
a reason to walk away.

00:19:12.300 --> 00:19:18.000
In my work i see some horrible things,

00:19:18.033 --> 00:19:20.768
Things that can't be explained.

00:19:20.801 --> 00:19:22.200
I deal with them.

00:19:22.234 --> 00:19:24.834
But working things out with you?

00:19:24.868 --> 00:19:27.501
I'm a scary one, all right.

00:19:27.534 --> 00:19:29.067
Hmm.

00:19:34.834 --> 00:19:39.434
Well, usually thgs get worked out

00:19:39.467 --> 00:19:42.234
When you really want them to.

00:19:46.534 --> 00:19:50.900
Yeah, but i'm still really
involved in my dad's work.

00:19:53.067 --> 00:19:58.601
No more excuses, okay? From you or me.

00:19:58.634 --> 00:19:59.834
Okay.

00:20:17.100 --> 00:20:19.900
Yeah

00:20:19.933 --> 00:20:23.033
You're kidding.

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:28.768
And he's with me.

00:20:30.768 --> 00:20:33.033
Where were you last night?

00:20:33.067 --> 00:20:36.067
You didn't make it back to the motel.

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:37.200
Nope.

00:20:37.234 --> 00:20:39.167
I'm guessing you guys worked things out.

00:20:39.200 --> 00:20:41.200
We'll be working things
out when we're 90.

00:20:41.234 --> 00:20:42.501
So, what happened?

00:20:42.534 --> 00:20:44.834
Every bone crushed, internal
organs turned to pudding.

00:20:44.868 --> 00:20:46.067
The cops are all stumped,

00:20:46.100 --> 00:20:47.967
But it's almost like
something ran him over.

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:49.534
Something like a truck? Yep.

00:20:49.567 --> 00:20:51.634
Tracks? Nope.

00:20:51.667 --> 00:20:53.734
What was the mayor doing here anyway?

00:20:53.768 --> 00:20:56.200
He owned the property.
Bought it a few weeks ago.

00:20:56.234 --> 00:20:58.367
Yeah, but he's white.
Doesn't fit the pattern.

00:20:58.401 --> 00:21:00.234
Killings didn't happen up on the road.

00:21:00.267 --> 00:21:03.134
That doesn't fit, either.

00:21:09.067 --> 00:21:10.334
Thanks.

00:21:10.367 --> 00:21:12.701
I'm trying to find some
link between those killings

00:21:12.734 --> 00:21:14.501
In the '60s and what's going on now.

00:21:14.534 --> 00:21:16.467
There wasn't a lot
about it in the paper.

00:21:16.501 --> 00:21:19.334
Not surprising. Probably
minimal-Police-Work deal.

00:21:19.367 --> 00:21:21.667
Back then, equal justice under the law

00:21:21.701 --> 00:21:23.601
Wasn't too literal around here.

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:27.367
Yeah?

00:21:27.401 --> 00:21:28.933
Sam: Okay, the courthouse records

00:21:28.967 --> 00:21:32.100
Show that mr. And mrs. Mayor
bought an abandoned property.

00:21:32.134 --> 00:21:34.100
The previous owner
was the dorian family,

00:21:34.134 --> 00:21:35.534
For like 150 years.

00:21:35.567 --> 00:21:36.868
Dorian? Yeah.

00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:39.300
Didn't you say the dorian
family used to own this paper?

00:21:39.334 --> 00:21:41.300
Along with most everything
else around here.

00:21:41.334 --> 00:21:43.467
Real pillars of the town.

00:21:43.501 --> 00:21:44.768
Right, right.

00:21:47.300 --> 00:21:48.734
That's interesting.

00:21:48.768 --> 00:21:50.701
What?

00:21:50.734 --> 00:21:53.801
This cyrus dorian, he
vanished in april of '63.

00:21:53.834 --> 00:21:56.801
The case was investigated
but never solved.

00:21:56.834 --> 00:21:59.167
It was the time the string
of murders was going on.

00:21:59.200 --> 00:22:00.868
Well, i pulled a bunch of
paper up on the dorian place.

00:22:00.900 --> 00:22:02.567
It must've been in bad shape
when the mayor bought it.

00:22:02.601 --> 00:22:04.100
Why is that?

00:22:04.134 --> 00:22:05.801
The first thing he did
was bulldoze the place.

00:22:05.834 --> 00:22:08.501
Mayor todd knocked down the dorianlace?

00:22:08.534 --> 00:22:12.200
It was a big deal. One of
the oldest local houses left.

00:22:12.234 --> 00:22:13.801
It made the front page.

00:22:13.834 --> 00:22:14.967
You got a date?

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:18.267
Uh... the 3rd of last month.

00:22:22.467 --> 00:22:25.933
Mayor todd bulldozed the
dorian family home on the 3rd.

00:22:25.967 --> 00:22:28.834
The first killing was the very next day.

00:23:51.300 --> 00:23:52.768
Dean!

00:23:56.980 --> 00:23:59.047
Maybe you could throw
a couple shots in that.

00:23:59.980 --> 00:24:03.714
You didn't see who
was driving the truck?

00:24:05.114 --> 00:24:06.514
It seemed to be no one.

00:24:09.413 --> 00:24:11.614
Everything was moving so fast.

00:24:13.317 --> 00:24:18.617
And then it was just gone.
Why didn't it kill us?

00:24:18.651 --> 00:24:22.317
Whatever is controlling the
truck wants you afraid first.

00:24:22.350 --> 00:24:27.517
Mrs. Robinson, cassie said
that your husband saw the truck

00:24:27.551 --> 00:24:30.183
Before he died.

00:24:30.217 --> 00:24:31.517
Mom?

00:24:31.551 --> 00:24:33.018
Hmm?

00:24:33.984 --> 00:24:36.851
Martin was under a lot of stress.

00:24:36.884 --> 00:24:38.851
You can't be sure about
what he was seeing.

00:24:38.884 --> 00:24:41.250
Well, after tonight i think
we can be reasonably sure

00:24:41.284 --> 00:24:42.651
That he was seeing a truck.

00:24:42.684 --> 00:24:47.984
What happened tonight, you
and cassie are marked, okay?

00:24:48.018 --> 00:24:50.350
Your daughter could die,
so if you know something,

00:24:50.384 --> 00:24:52.317
Now would be a really good
time to tell us about it.

00:24:52.350 --> 00:24:54.217
Dean... yes.

00:24:54.250 --> 00:24:56.918
Yes, he said he saw a truck.

00:24:56.951 --> 00:24:59.150
Did he know who it belonged to?

00:24:59.183 --> 00:25:01.484
He thought he did. Who was that?

00:25:03.551 --> 00:25:06.517
Cyrus...

00:25:06.551 --> 00:25:09.617
A man named cyrus.

00:25:12.951 --> 00:25:15.350
Is this cyrus?

00:25:15.384 --> 00:25:20.984
Cyrus dorian died
more than 40 years ago.

00:25:21.018 --> 00:25:25.284
How do you know he died, mrs. Robinson?

00:25:26.984 --> 00:25:29.183
The paper said he went missing.

00:25:29.217 --> 00:25:31.551
How do you know he died?

00:25:31.584 --> 00:25:35.217
We were all very young.

00:25:37.217 --> 00:25:40.083
I dated cyrus a while.

00:25:40.117 --> 00:25:43.183
I was also seeing martin,
in secret of course

00:25:43.217 --> 00:25:49.450
'Cause interracial couples
didn't go over too well then.

00:25:49.484 --> 00:25:51.984
When i broke it off with cyrus,

00:25:52.018 --> 00:25:54.918
And when he found out about martin...

00:25:54.951 --> 00:26:00.417
I don't know... he changed.

00:26:00.450 --> 00:26:06.250
His hatred... his
hatred was frightening.

00:26:06.284 --> 00:26:07.751
The string of murders.

00:26:07.784 --> 00:26:10.250
There were rumors,

00:26:10.284 --> 00:26:13.117
People of color disappearing
into some kind oa truck.

00:26:16.484 --> 00:26:19.217
Nothing was ever done.

00:26:24.517 --> 00:26:26.417
Martin and...

00:26:28.417 --> 00:26:32.717
Martin and i, we were gonna be married

00:26:32.751 --> 00:26:34.751
In that little church near here,

00:26:34.784 --> 00:26:37.684
But last minute, we decided to elope

00:26:37.717 --> 00:26:40.018
'Cause we didn't want all the attention.

00:26:40.050 --> 00:26:41.284
And cyrus?

00:26:48.018 --> 00:26:53.317
The day we set for the wedding

00:26:53.350 --> 00:26:58.884
Was the day someone
set fire to the church.

00:27:06.984 --> 00:27:12.183
There was a children's
choir practicing in there.

00:27:14.651 --> 00:27:17.784
They all died.

00:27:20.217 --> 00:27:22.784
Did the attacks stop after that?

00:27:22.817 --> 00:27:25.751
No, there was one more.

00:27:27.751 --> 00:27:32.551
One night that truck came for martin.

00:27:35.018 --> 00:27:37.484
Cyrus beat him something terrible,

00:27:42.183 --> 00:27:45.384
But martin... you see, martin got loose

00:27:45.417 --> 00:27:48.250
And he started hitting cyrus

00:27:48.284 --> 00:27:52.484
And he just kept hitting
him and hitting him.

00:28:03.751 --> 00:28:06.083
Why didn't you call the cops?

00:28:10.417 --> 00:28:13.617
This was 40 years ago.

00:28:13.651 --> 00:28:17.250
He called on his friends...

00:28:17.284 --> 00:28:19.217
Clayton, solmes, and jimmy anderson...

00:28:19.250 --> 00:28:22.584
And they put cyrus' body into the truck

00:28:22.617 --> 00:28:27.183
And then rolled it into the
swamp at the edge of his land

00:28:27.217 --> 00:28:33.717
And all three of them kept
that secret all these years.

00:28:35.751 --> 00:28:37.183
And now all three are gone.

00:28:37.217 --> 00:28:38.317
So is mayor todd.

00:28:40.083 --> 00:28:43.384
Now, he said that you of all people

00:28:43.417 --> 00:28:45.217
Would know that he is not a racist.

00:28:45.250 --> 00:28:46.284
Why would he say that?

00:28:46.317 --> 00:28:47.317
He was a good man.

00:28:47.350 --> 00:28:50.617
He was a young deputy back then,

00:28:50.651 --> 00:28:52.384
Investigating cyrus's disappearance.

00:28:52.417 --> 00:28:58.117
Once he figured out what
martin and the others had done,

00:28:58.150 --> 00:29:03.951
He he did nothing

00:29:05.617 --> 00:29:08.684
Because he also knew
what cyrus had done.

00:29:11.817 --> 00:29:13.484
Why didn't you tell me?

00:29:13.517 --> 00:29:16.183
I thought i was protecting them.

00:29:18.250 --> 00:29:23.350
And now there's no one left to protect.

00:29:23.384 --> 00:29:24.751
Yes, there is.

00:29:34.018 --> 00:29:36.117
Oh, my life was so simple.

00:29:36.150 --> 00:29:40.617
Just school, exams,

00:29:40.651 --> 00:29:44.150
Papers on polycentric cultural norms.

00:29:44.183 --> 00:29:48.083
So i guess i saved you
from a boring existence.

00:29:48.117 --> 00:29:50.284
Occasionally i miss boring.

00:29:52.050 --> 00:29:53.617
So, this killer truck...

00:29:53.651 --> 00:29:57.517
I miss conversations that didn't
start with "this killer truck."

00:29:57.551 --> 00:29:59.984
Ah...

00:30:00.018 --> 00:30:01.951
All right, well, this cyrus guy,

00:30:01.984 --> 00:30:04.617
Evil on a level that
infected even his truck.

00:30:04.651 --> 00:30:08.150
When he died, the swamp became his tomb

00:30:08.183 --> 00:30:10.517
And his spirit was dormant for 40 years.

00:30:10.551 --> 00:30:11.751
So, what woke it up?

00:30:11.784 --> 00:30:14.350
The construction on his
house or the destructi.

00:30:14.384 --> 00:30:15.484
Right.

00:30:15.517 --> 00:30:18.284
Demolition or remodeling
can awaken spirits,

00:30:18.317 --> 00:30:20.018
Make them restless.

00:30:20.050 --> 00:30:22.417
Like that theater in illinois.

00:30:22.450 --> 00:30:23.684
Yeah.

00:30:23.717 --> 00:30:25.717
And the guy who tears
down the family homestead,

00:30:25.751 --> 00:30:28.250
Harold todd, is the same guy

00:30:28.284 --> 00:30:31.817
That kept cyrus's murder
quiet and unsolved.

00:30:31.851 --> 00:30:34.018
So now his spirit is
awakened and out for blood.

00:30:34.050 --> 00:30:36.317
I guess. Who knows what
ghosts are thinking anyway.

00:30:36.350 --> 00:30:39.717
You know we're gonna have to
dredge that body from the swamp?

00:30:39.751 --> 00:30:41.350
Maman.

00:30:41.384 --> 00:30:43.717
You said it. Yeah.

00:30:43.751 --> 00:30:44.717
Hey.

00:30:44.751 --> 00:30:45.717
Hey.

00:30:45.751 --> 00:30:47.784
She's asleep.

00:30:47.817 --> 00:30:49.884
Now what?

00:30:49.918 --> 00:30:51.617
You stay put and look after her.

00:30:51.651 --> 00:30:53.717
And we'll be back.
Don't leave the house.

00:30:53.751 --> 00:30:55.951
Don't go getting all
authoritative on me.

00:30:55.984 --> 00:30:57.050
I hate it.

00:30:58.484 --> 00:31:01.217
Don't leave the house, please?

00:31:13.183 --> 00:31:15.918
You coming or what?

00:31:20.517 --> 00:31:24.117
Sam: All right, let's get her up.

00:31:25.684 --> 00:31:28.918
All right. Little more.

00:31:28.951 --> 00:31:30.183
Little more.

00:31:31.450 --> 00:31:33.651
Litt more.

00:31:33.684 --> 00:31:34.918
All right, stop.

00:31:43.551 --> 00:31:44.684
Nice.

00:31:44.717 --> 00:31:46.784
Hell yeah.

00:31:46.817 --> 00:31:48.183
Now i know what she sees in you.

00:31:48.217 --> 00:31:49.450
What?

00:31:49.484 --> 00:31:52.018
Come on, you can admit it.
You're still in love with her.

00:31:52.050 --> 00:31:53.317
Can we focus, please?

00:31:53.350 --> 00:31:55.183
I'm just saying, dean.

00:31:55.217 --> 00:31:56.217
Hold that.

00:31:56.250 --> 00:31:58.851
All right. What am i getting?

00:31:58.884 --> 00:32:00.450
Gas, flashlight. Got it, got it.

00:32:00.484 --> 00:32:01.984
All right, let's get this done.

00:32:02.018 --> 00:32:04.250
All right. Got it.

00:32:21.551 --> 00:32:23.083
All right, let's get to it.

00:32:38.651 --> 00:32:41.250
Think that'll do it?

00:32:47.083 --> 00:32:49.050
I guess not.

00:32:52.677 --> 00:32:54.577
So burning the body had
no effect on that thing?

00:32:54.610 --> 00:32:55.944
Sure it did. Now it's really pissed.

00:32:55.977 --> 00:32:57.910
But cyrus's ghost is gone, right, dean?

00:32:57.944 --> 00:32:59.710
Apparently not the part
that's fused with the truck.

00:32:59.984 --> 00:33:01.783
Where you going?

00:33:01.817 --> 00:33:04.184
Going for a little ride.
Gonna lead that thing away.

00:33:04.217 --> 00:33:06.017
That rusted piece of
crap, you got to burn it.

00:33:06.050 --> 00:33:07.651
How the hell am i supposed
to burn a truck, dean?

00:33:07.684 --> 00:33:09.517
I don't know. Figure something out.

00:33:09.891 --> 00:33:11.524
Figure something...

00:33:51.421 --> 00:33:53.588
Hey, you got to give me a minute.

00:33:53.620 --> 00:33:55.121
I don't have a minute!
What are we doing?!

00:33:55.154 --> 00:33:58.121
Uh... let me get back to you.

00:34:00.588 --> 00:34:02.121
Hey, cassie? Hey, it's sam.

00:34:02.154 --> 00:34:05.187
Okay, i need some information
and it has to be exactly right.

00:34:08.454 --> 00:34:10.154
All right, dean. This better be good!

00:34:10.187 --> 00:34:13.787
Where are you? I'm in the middle of
nowhere with a killer truck on my ass!

00:34:13.820 --> 00:34:16.020
It's like it knows i
put the torch to cyrus!

00:34:16.054 --> 00:34:17.720
Dean, listen to me. It's important.

00:34:17.753 --> 00:34:18.820
I have to know exactly where you are.

00:34:18.854 --> 00:34:21.254
Decatur road, about two
miles off the highway.

00:34:21.287 --> 00:34:23.054
Okay, headed east? Yes!

00:34:27.987 --> 00:34:31.187
Oh, you son of a bitch.

00:34:31.221 --> 00:34:32.454
Okay, uh, turn right.

00:34:39.454 --> 00:34:40.653
You make the turn?

00:34:40.687 --> 00:34:42.087
Yeah, i made the turn!

00:34:42.121 --> 00:34:43.854
Move this thing along a little faster!

00:34:43.887 --> 00:34:45.454
All right, you see a road up ahead?

00:34:45.488 --> 00:34:46.687
No!

00:34:46.720 --> 00:34:48.454
Wait, yes, i see it!

00:34:48.488 --> 00:34:50.087
Okay, turn left. What?!

00:34:57.588 --> 00:34:59.154
All right, now what?

00:34:59.187 --> 00:35:01.154
Go exactly 7/10ths of a mile and stop.

00:35:01.187 --> 00:35:03.854
Stop? Exactly 7/10ths, dean.

00:35:03.887 --> 00:35:06.254
7/10ths, 7/10ths.

00:35:35.720 --> 00:35:38.554
Dean, are you still there?

00:35:38.588 --> 00:35:40.254
Yeah. What's happening?

00:35:40.287 --> 00:35:42.254
It's just staring at me. What do i do?

00:35:42.287 --> 00:35:44.653
Just what you are doing...
bringing it to you.

00:35:44.687 --> 00:35:45.753
Wh...

00:36:02.820 --> 00:36:04.354
Come on, come on.

00:36:24.387 --> 00:36:27.054
Dean?

00:36:27.087 --> 00:36:28.287
You still there?

00:36:28.321 --> 00:36:31.154
Dean?

00:36:31.187 --> 00:36:33.588
Where'd it go?

00:36:33.620 --> 00:36:36.820
Dean, you're where the church was.

00:36:36.854 --> 00:36:38.087
What church?

00:36:38.121 --> 00:36:40.588
The place cyrus burned down
and murdered all those kids.

00:36:40.620 --> 00:36:42.221
There's not a whole lot left.

00:36:42.254 --> 00:36:43.954
Church ground is hallowed ground

00:36:43.987 --> 00:36:45.488
Whether the church
is still there or not.

00:36:45.521 --> 00:36:47.554
Evil spirits cross over hallowed ground,

00:36:47.588 --> 00:36:49.321
Sometimes they're destroyed.

00:36:49.354 --> 00:36:54.254
So i figured maybe that
would get rid of it.

00:36:54.287 --> 00:36:55.287
Maybe?

00:36:55.321 --> 00:36:56.620
Maybe?!

00:36:56.653 --> 00:36:59.354
What if you were wrong?!

00:37:01.121 --> 00:37:03.820
Honestly, that thought
hadn't occurred to me.

00:37:08.020 --> 00:37:10.321
"Well, that honestly
didn't occur to me."

00:37:16.321 --> 00:37:17.987
I'm gonna kill him.

00:37:24.974 --> 00:37:28.007
My mother says to tell you thanks again.

00:37:32.940 --> 00:37:35.841
This was a better goodbye
than the last time.

00:37:35.874 --> 00:37:37.808
Yeah, well, maybe this time

00:37:37.841 --> 00:37:40.107
It'll be a little less permanent.

00:37:40.140 --> 00:37:43.707
You know what?

00:37:43.741 --> 00:37:46.741
I'm a realist.

00:37:46.774 --> 00:37:49.707
I don't see much hope for us, dean.

00:37:53.374 --> 00:37:56.240
Well, i've seen stranger things happen.

00:37:56.274 --> 00:37:57.940
Hell of a lot stranger.

00:38:02.607 --> 00:38:04.474
Goodbye, dean.

00:38:04.507 --> 00:38:07.474
I'll see you, cassie.

00:38:07.507 --> 00:38:10.441
I will.

00:39:03.007 --> 00:39:05.107
I like her.

00:39:05.140 --> 00:39:06.474
Yeah.

00:39:08.808 --> 00:39:10.574
You meet someone like her,

00:39:10.607 --> 00:39:13.407
Ever make you wonder if it's worth it...

00:39:13.441 --> 00:39:17.541
Putting everything else
on hold, doing what we do?

00:39:30.107 --> 00:39:33.207
Why don't you wake me up
when it's my turn to drive?



00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.000
